Here is the commit message:
LUCENE-7698: fix CommonGramsQueryFilter to not produce a
 disconnected token graph

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the `CommonGramsQueryFilter` producing a disconnected token graph when processing tokens, which occurred because the position length of tokens was not being set correctly. This led to issues in phrase queries during query parsing, as the token graph was not properly connected, resulting in incorrect query results.

Here is the patch:
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.TokenFilter;
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.tokenattributes.PositionIncrementAttribute;
+import org.apache.lucene.analysis.tokenattributes.PositionLengthAttribute;
