Reason:
The bug occurs because the `CommonGramsQueryFilter` does not correctly set the position length of tokens when processing them. When the `isGramType()` condition is not met, the previous token state is restored without adjusting the position length, which can lead to a disconnected token graph. This improper handling results in incorrect phrase queries during query parsing.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
posLengthAttribute.setPositionLength(1);
```
```java
if (isGramType()) {
    posLengthAttribute.setPositionLength(1);
}
```
Reason:
The fix involves explicitly setting the position length of tokens to 1 when they are of gram type. This ensures that the token graph remains connected, preventing the disconnection issue that was causing incorrect query results. By ensuring the position length is correctly set, the token graph can accurately represent the relationships between tokens in phrase queries.

